 as calling saveBitmapImageToFile(). Wdyt?"],["43537716_67b1090b",22,0,0,"This may block UI thread too, should we move it to background thread?"],["78dc85a0_e222af07",22,0,1,"This method is no longer about background image file. How about renaming it to saveBitmapImageToFile()?"],["9b853348_8dee96f2",22,0,1,"createBackgroundImageFile()?"],["c2c4dd36_8af1d8ff",22,0,1,"Rename this to saveBitmapImageToFileImpl()?"],["da7139b5_c0c2089f",22,0,1,"Log.i."]],0,284],[7247786,20432,19,0.721,0.543,[[0,40]],[],0,285],[7248369,20433,294,7.579,6.176,[[0,1.0,41,292]],[["08c0d765_9f853ae4",52,0,1,"Nit: Can we add a local variable for 1L?"],["3a651542_a50c0264",49,0,1,"saves -> save?"],["3d957265_1c20f9ab",42,0,1,"Suggest to split this test as two: testMaybeUpdateDailyRefreshTimestamp_chromeColor() and testMaybeUpdateDailyRefreshTimestamp_themeCollection()."],["a7c154f7_9bf62f32",51,0,0,"Out of curiosity, do we need to check currentInfo.isDailyRefreshEnabled?"],["c6e848ac_200e6e76",22,0,0,"Will it be possible to check sharedPreference as the way what chrome colors does? Thus, you don't need to pass in customBackgroundInfo. It's fine that you don't add the SharedPreference key in this…"]],0,286],[7260936,20437,47,1.326,1.047,[[0,42]],[],0,287],[7253170,20437,17,0.662,0.495,[[24,0.737,0,13],[0,0.263,43,4]],[["537cc65d_a8bc4d08",53,-4,1,"Maybe we need to have a new label for Android."]],0,288],[7254199,20438,660,10.952,8.912,[[0,0.975,44,641],[18,0.025,115,15]],[["3093798f_47f3c9f0",22,-1,1,"I feel it's better not mixing with other cases. How about: if (imageType == NtpBackgroundImageType.THEME_COLLECTION) { color = ...; } else { color = getCustomizedPrimaryColorFromSharedPreference() }"],["30f9cc84_35197282",54,-1,1,"We only need to save a status to tell other class that an daily refresh is applied. All other loading can be done in configManager."],["3c461a8c_150908e4",22,-1,1,"After a second thought, how do you feel about simply using two files in turn if daily update is enabled, lik